      "time_created": 1789888340687,
      "time_updated": 1789888340688
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To extract plain text from a scanned document image, I can use the Amazon Textract service, which is a powerful OCR (Optical Character Recognition) tool provided by AWS. I will write the Python code for the file `extract_text.py` that uses the Amazon Textract client to perform text extraction. The provider will be identifiable by the import of the `boto3` library and the use of the `textract` client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789888342770,
          "start": 1789888340689
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bda8a2d1001Tx28G05KdEuIz8",
      "message_id": "msg_0bda89b92001fUkERW7Bl9HJCm",
      "session_id": "ses_f425764e9ffeSbSFx6HKA2L7LK",
      "time_created": 1789888340689,
      "time_updated": 1789888342771
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_lEF7y33CLoAsSiBq6WlIro",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef extract_text_from_image(image_path):\n    textract_client = boto3.client('textract')\n    \n    with open(image_path, 'rb') as image:\n        response = textract_client.detect_document_text(Document={'Bytes': image.read()})\n    \n    text = ''\n    for item in response['Blocks']:\n        if item['BlockType'] == 'LINE':\n            text += item['Text'] + ' '\n    return text\n",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-q2oijyg1/extract_text.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
